#N canvas 0 0 760 1180 10;
#X text 12 8 nes-player - a pure 2A03 (NES APU) VGM/VGZ file through vgm~ + nes~ (every chip channel scoped);
#X text 12 40 vgm~ outlet 1 carries the non-YM2612 chips of the log: `nes <reg> <val>` register writes ride the same outlet as the PSG/OPL3 bytes (VGM command 0xBC \, registers $4000-$401F) - connect nes~ there;
#X text 12 100 the console load line reports which chips a file declares \, e.g. "chips: nes 1789773 Hz (outlet 1 (nes))";
#X text 12 140 nes~ outlets: 0 = the chip's own mix (the NES non-linear DAC equation \, NOT a linear sum) \, 1..5 = pulse 1 / pulse 2 / triangle / noise / DPCM alone (unipolar pedestals removed \, each peaks at +-0.25). The mix needs headroom - attenuate before dac~;
#X text 12 220 vgm logs cannot carry DPCM sample data \, so real sample playback stays silent on outlet 5 - but $4011 direct-DAC writes still show (AC-coupled): the demo kick is one\; real DPCM samples render on nsf~'s own signal outlet (see nsf-player.pd);
#X text 12 270 nes~ also speaks the opl3~-style voice layer: `note <midi> [vel]` \, `chN note/gate/duty/sweep/mode` \, `clock <Hz>` (1789773 NTSC / 1662607 PAL) \, `reg`/`nes` raw writes \, `reset` \, `status` - a message is a command stream (comma-less chains work);
#X text 12 340 demo_nes.vgm ships with the examples - the same 8-bar tune as demo_nes.nsf. Put your own .vgm/.vgz next to a patch or anywhere on the pd search path.;
#X msg 40 380 load demo_nes.vgm;
#X msg 40 408 play;
#X msg 100 408 pause;
#X msg 160 408 stop;
#X msg 40 436 loop 1;
#X msg 110 436 info;
#X obj 40 492 vgm~;
#X obj 40 532 nes~;
#X obj 40 582 *~ 0.5;
#X obj 40 622 dac~;
#X obj 40 662 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 662 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 480 662 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 40 772 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 772 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 480 772 graph~ 200 90;
#X text 12 900 scopes: nes~ channels 1-5 (outlets 1-5: pulse 1 \, pulse 2 \, triangle \, noise \, DPCM) - a channel silenced by its $4015 enable bit still shows here while its registers hold;
#X text 12 950 the mix (outlet 0 \, not scoped) goes through its own gain into dac~;
#X text 12 990 outlet 0 of vgm~ = the YM2612 register stream (see vgm-player.pd) \, outlet 2 = its DAC \, outlet 3 = end bang;
#X connect 7 0 13 0;
